---
import '../home.css';
const title = 'Mydroid – Your Android phone on your Mac';
const description = 'Reply to texts, answer calls, and sync photos between Android and Mac. Free, open source, and no account needed.';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  <meta name="description" content={description} />
  <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
  <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  <link rel="canonical" href={new URL('/', Astro.site)} />
</head>
<body class="surface">
    <header class="site-head">
      <div class="site-head-inner">
        <a class="brand" href="/"><img src="/favicon.svg" width="29" height="29" alt="">Mydroid</a>
        <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Website">
          <a href="#features" class="desktop-only">Features</a>
          <a href="/get-started/">Guides</a>
          <a href="/get-started/build-from-source/">Build from source</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/gautamm20/mydroid">GitHub</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

  <main id="main">
    <div class="wrap">
      <section class="hero">
        <h1>Your Android phone on your Mac</h1>
        <p>Reply to a text, answer a call, or find a photo you just took, all from your Mac. Send files and links in either direction over your own Wi‑Fi.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn" href="/get-started/install-mac/">Install on Mac</a>
          <a class="btn secondary" href="/get-started/install-android/">Get the Android app</a>
        </div>
        <p class="requirements">Free and open source. No account needed.</p>
      </section>
      <figure class="hero-image">
        <img class="hero-mac" src="/screenshots/mac-messages.webp" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" alt="A text conversation from an Android phone open in Mydroid for Mac">
        <img class="hero-phone" src="/screenshots/android-home.webp" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The linked Mac and sharing actions in Mydroid for Android">
      </figure>
      <nav class="feature-nav" aria-label="Jump to a feature" id="features">
        <a href="#feature-photos">Photos</a>
        <a href="#feature-messages">Messages</a>
        <a href="#feature-calls">Calls</a>
        <a href="#feature-files">Files</a>
        <a href="#feature-clipboard">Clipboard and links</a>
        <a href="#feature-remote">Remote</a>
        <a href="#feature-auth">Authenticator</a>
      </nav>
    </div>

    <section class="wrap feature expanded" id="feature-photos">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <h2>Find the photo you just took</h2>
        <p>New camera photos show up in Pictures → Mydroid. Open Photos in Mydroid on your Mac when you need an older shot.</p>
        <ul><li>Save original files.</li><li>Import into Apple Photos if you prefer.</li><li>Transfers pick up again when the phone reconnects.</li></ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/photos-and-files/">Set up photo sync</a>
      </div>
      <figure class="feature-figure">
        <div class="visual"><img class="frame" src="/screenshots/mac-photos.webp" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Mac photo browser with a camera roll and Save to Pictures selected"></div>
        <figcaption class="caption">Browse the camera roll and save the originals you want.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap feature flip" id="feature-messages">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <h2>Reply while your phone stays in your pocket</h2>
        <p>Phone notifications appear on your Mac. Reply when the Android app offers it, or dismiss a notification on both devices at once.</p>
        <ul><li>Read and send SMS from the Messages window.</li><li>See app chats as their notifications arrive.</li><li>Mute individual apps or set quiet hours.</li></ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/messages-and-calls/">Turn on messages and notifications</a>
      </div>
      <figure class="feature-figure">
        <div class="visual blue stack"><img class="frame" src="/screenshots/mac-messages.webp" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Mydroid Messages window with an SMS conversation"><img src="/screenshots/mac-notification.webp" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="An Android Gmail notification on the Mac"></div>
        <figcaption class="caption">Texts and Android app alerts both reach your Mac.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap feature" id="feature-calls">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <h2>See who’s calling</h2>
        <p>Answer, decline, or start a cellular call from the Mac. With standard setup, you talk and listen on your phone.</p>
        <p>Mac mic and speaker support is an optional setup on compatible phones. It uses Android wireless debugging and your existing adb.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/messages-and-calls/#calls">Hear calls on your Mac</a>
      </div>
      <figure class="feature-figure">
        <div class="visual stack"><img src="/screenshots/mac-incoming-call.webp" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="An incoming call on the Mac showing the caller and answer controls"><img src="/screenshots/mac-call-audio.webp" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="A connected call showing Mac audio controls"></div>
        <figcaption class="caption">The incoming-call panel and the optional Mac audio controls.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap feature flip" id="feature-files">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <h2>Send a file either way</h2>
        <p>Share a file to Mydroid from Android, or drop it on the menu bar to send it back. Incoming files land in Downloads.</p>
        <ul><li>Receive from Android’s Quick Share menu.</li><li>Open the Mac folders you’ve shared from your phone.</li><li>Choose which folders the phone can write to.</li></ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/photos-and-files/">Move photos and files</a>
      </div>
      <figure class="feature-figure">
        <div class="visual"><img class="frame" src="/screenshots/mac-files.webp" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Mac Files window with received files and transfer sizes"></div>
        <figcaption class="caption">Find received files and see what’s still transferring.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap feature" id="feature-clipboard">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <h2>Pick up a link on the other screen</h2>
        <p>Share a link from your phone to open it in the Mac’s browser. Send a link the other way when it’s time to leave your desk.</p>
        <p>Turn on clipboard sharing to copy text on one device and paste on the other. You can leave it off and share individual items.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/clipboard-and-links/">Copy text and share links</a>
      </div>
      <figure class="feature-figure">
        <div class="visual blue stack"><img src="/screenshots/mac-open-link.webp" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="A link from Android appears on the Mac with an Open action"><img src="/screenshots/mac-copied-text.webp" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="A Mac notification confirms text copied from the phone"></div>
        <figcaption class="caption">Open a link from your phone, or paste text you copied there.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap feature flip" id="feature-remote">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <h2>Control the Mac from across the room</h2>
        <p>Use your phone as a trackpad, change the music, or advance a slide without standing next to the Mac.</p>
        <ul><li>Type, scroll, and switch apps.</li><li>Present with slide controls, a timer, and Keynote speaker notes.</li><li>Open Mac apps and shared files from Android.</li><li>Lock, sleep, or ring from the phone. Turn on Walk-away lock if you want the Mac to lock automatically.</li></ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/remote-and-lock/">Use the remote</a>
      </div>
      <figure class="feature-figure">
        <div class="visual phones"><img src="/screenshots/android-presenter.webp" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Android presenter view with slide controls and a timer"><img src="/screenshots/android-trackpad.webp" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Android trackpad with keyboard and Mac shortcuts"></div>
        <figcaption class="caption">Run a presentation or use the trackpad from your phone.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap feature" id="feature-auth">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <h2>Fill a sign-in code from your phone</h2>
        <p>Choose Fill from phone in Chrome and approve on Android. The code appears in the sign-in form and your authenticator keys stay on the phone.</p>
        <ul><li>Choose which sites show the fill button.</li><li>Use ⌃⌥C when you need a code outside the extension.</li><li>Import accounts from Google Authenticator.</li></ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/authenticator/">Set up Mydroid Authenticator</a>
      </div>
      <figure class="feature-figure">
        <div class="visual sand"><img src="/screenshots/chrome-fill.webp" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Mydroid Fill from phone button below a verification-code field"></div>
        <figcaption class="caption">The fill button appears under the verification-code field on sites you allow.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap install">
      <h2>Install Mydroid, then scan to pair</h2>
      <div class="install-row">
        <article><strong>1. On your Mac</strong><h3>Install Mydroid</h3><p>Run one command in Terminal. Mydroid opens in your menu bar.</p><a class="text-link" href="/get-started/install-mac/">Mac install guide</a></article>
        <article><strong>2. On Android</strong><h3>Get the APK</h3><p>Download the app and open the file on your phone.</p><a class="text-link" href="/get-started/install-android/">Android install guide</a></article>
        <article><strong>3. On both devices</strong><h3>Pair your phone</h3><p>Join the same Wi‑Fi, scan the Mac’s QR code, and choose what to sync.</p><a class="text-link" href="/get-started/pair/">Pairing guide</a></article>
      </div>
      <p class="source-install">Want to compile the apps yourself? <a class="text-link" href="/get-started/build-from-source/">Build Mydroid from source</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
    <footer class="trust-line"><div class="site-footer-inner"><span>Your phone and Mac sync directly, over an encrypted connection.</span><div class="actions"><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a><a href="https://github.com/gautamm20/mydroid">Source on GitHub</a></div></div></footer>
</body>
</html>
